export anchor CodeEditorLightStyle:
    number: 57
    screen: Inbox
    name: Code editor light
    idea: The inbox opens like files in a light code editor, with a file tree for filters, tabs for open items, numbered lines and syntax colours that tell names, verbs, titles and times apart.
    base: light
    palette:
        chrome: #eceef2, the title bar, tab strip and activity bar
        side: #f5f6f8, the file tree and the reply panel
        editor: #ffffff, the editor panes
        selection: #e6eefc, the open line and the active file
        text: #24292f, default code text
        dim: #5c6570, breadcrumbs and inactive tabs
        function: #0a5bb5, person names, the primary button, links and focus
        keyword: #8a2bb5, verbs and the at mention
        string: #0f6e3a, quoted task titles and the done tag
        number: #a14a00, times and dates
        comment: #5f6b5a, projects and comment lines in italic
        error: #b42318, unread tags and the unread count
        status: #2d4b8a, the status bar with white text
    type:
        Code is ui-monospace, SF Mono, Cascadia Code, JetBrains Mono,
        Menlo, Consolas, DejaVu Sans Mono, monospace at 13px on a 1.6 line
        height. Priya's message alone is in system-ui at 15px on a 1.55
        line height. Breadcrumbs are 12px, tags 11px bold, and panel
        headings 11px semibold system-ui uppercase.
    layout:
        A window 1280px wide at most with a title bar of three grey dots,
        the app name, a command field reading Go to task, project or person
        and mara.okafor. Below sit a 44px activity bar of icons, a 220px
        Explorer tree with an inbox folder holding all, mentions, assigned
        and unread with 3 U, and the editor. The editor has tabs for
        inbox/all and hero-image-options with an unread dot, then two split
        panes. The left pane lists the inbox as numbered lines between a
        header comment and an end comment, each line reading name, verb,
        quoted title, project as a comment, time and tags. The right pane
        shows from and task lines, the message in a pale yellow note box,
        an attachments comment and three thumbnails with Option labels. A
        Reply panel under both panes has a prompt field and buttons with
        keyboard hints, and a blue status bar closes the window. Below
        1000px the tree becomes a strip of file links and the panes stack.
        Below 600px the activity bar turns into a top row.
    spacing: A 4px unit. 21px code lines, 12px pane gutters, 44px line number gutter.
    density: High. One notification per numbered line.
    corners: 8px on the window, 4px on note boxes and thumbnails, 3px on buttons, fields and tags.
    borders: 1px #d5d9e0 between every region, a 2px accent line on top of the active tab and at the left of the selected line.
    shadows: Only the window, 0 8px 24px rgba(30,40,60,0.12).
    icons:
        16px thin line icons with a 1.6 stroke, tinted by kind, orange for
        folders and blue for files. Tags are small outlined boxes, a dot
        with unread, a tick with done and a triangle with open. Buttons
        carry keyboard hints in small key boxes.
    focus: A 1px accent outline with a soft 3 to 4px accent ring. A focused field gets an accent border and the same ring.
    tone: Lowercase paths and code comments, such as inbox › all, // end of inbox and reply to Priya.
